d now I don't know how much  time we have well  early questions  [Music]  right and I think that that was the  important part of asking for a  refinement instead of buying from day  one so every city's gonna be different  but I think what was really important in  our process was not going to the powers  that be until we had a product to share  and saying what do you think yeah yeah  could this be useful do you want to be  involved you want us to launch this just  as citizens doing a side thing and they  were like nah we wanted what more data  do you need you know but it wasn't until  we had something to look at it otherwise  it's a waste of time to have these  hypothetical conversations about what  you may or may not provide yeah so in a  more concrete example for your use case  would be rather than coming to the city  and asking for a change in process come  to them and be like we built you this  app we want you to use this to collect  data now because your papers are  annoying  [Music]  we get a lot of like how what if we want  to click on a property and input our own  information are like upload a photo or  say found one you know put it in the  system and right now we're really  focused on how do we automate what we  have because this is we're always  chasing our tail right so property  ownership changes and inspections come  in and condemnation zand and out and so  what we're trying to focus on right now  anyway is is a constant single source of  truth of where every vacant property is  that's updated automatically and when we  get to that point then how do we feed in  input and kind of ground efforts if that  answers your question  so hopefully yes but we want to get past  this phase one first wrong finger oh  thank you I'm gonna answer that one no  we you know we have this conversation  with people a lot actually about you  know if you're just taking all the  information that there is and turning  around and pushing it out into the world  without any kind of f